  "findings": [],
  "source_checks": [
    "Read every changed source and test. Borrowed preflight shares PropsBudget node/byte/depth accounting with owned constructor; nested objects count the same object and value nodes, string/key lengths include the same eight-byte charges. All properties preflight before owned allocation; count checks precede scanning.",
    "Ordered object keys are explicitly strict and duplicate-free before BTreeMap materialization, including nested objects. Source/entity ordering and duplicate/source membership checks remain in ScriptBindings::new. Aggregate row properties share a single budget.",
    "NumberBits/from_bits preserves every admitted finite f64 bit pattern, including signed zero and subnormal; nonfinite values refuse. UTF-8/control/quote/backslash data uses Rust Debug string literals rather than executable interpolation.",
    "Emission uses bounded validated catalog data in const borrowed slices and one common from_embedded call. Existing unsafe CompiledScript executable trust crossing, metadata hashes, exact bindings fingerprint and runtime immutable property construction remain unchanged.",
    "Reviewed actual generated consumer source plus retained compile/execute logs and hashes. It checks every one of 10000 ordered rows, every mixed value kind, negative zero, complete binding fingerprint and trusted artifact metadata. It does not run a 10000-entity game tick; separate public host test executes borrowed properties through two real ScriptHost ticks.",
    "No manifest/lock/dependency or default feature changes; six-path source scope is exact. Shared bindings.rs change is limited to budget visibility/text_size, independent of pending BoundGroup cache."
  ],
